    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d843-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d843-f1-content">
                <p>Plenary position papers were always prepared for the instruction of the U.S.
                    Delegation’s voting. They were drafted by the delegation staff in consultation
                    with the delegation members, in light of the situation obtaining after final
                    action had been taken on a given agenda item by the appropriate committee, in
                    this case the Fourth Committee. This documentation ordinarily is found only in
                    the documentation of IO file, lot 71 D 440, “General Assembly Delegations
                    (1946–1965)”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d843-f2" n="2" xml:id="d843-f2-content">
